      <p>A complete breakdown of nonstop coverage from Canada's four major airports — which routes are year-round, which are seasonal, and which destinations require a connection no matter what airline you use.</p>
      <h3><a href="/blog/nonstop-flights-worth-extra-cost">Are Nonstop Flights Worth the Extra Cost?</a></h3>
      <p>The premium for nonstop is real but often smaller than travelers expect — typically 0 to 40 percent depending on route and timing. A four-question decision framework helps you know when to pay it and when to take the connection.</p>
      <h3><a href="/blog/longest-nonstop-flights-world">The Longest Nonstop Flights in the World</a></h3>
